<h2 class="mt-14">Consent and purchaser suppression for Segmentation</h2>
<p>For segmentation, audit consent capture and purchase-event suppression before the first flow goes live — every app must record segmentation opt-ins you can evidence and halt promos at checkout. In segmentation, mistimed sends after purchases, refunds, or support cases destroy channel value quicker than any creative miss.</p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto mb-8"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Audience state</th><th>Required handling</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>No documented consent</td><td>Hold all segmentation marketing; transactional only</td><td>Consent evidence underwrites all segmentation sending</td></tr>
<tr><td>Consented, never purchased</td><td>Lead segmentation newcomers with teaching and social proof</td><td>Early segmentation discounts train deal-waiting</td></tr>
<tr><td>Active cart, no checkout</td><td>Context-rich segmentation nudge before any incentive</td><td>Segmentation high-intent window deserves margin discipline</td></tr>
<tr><td>Purchased recently</td><td>Suppress segmentation selling after checkout; educate instead</td><td>Post-checkout segmentation pitches trigger regret and opt-outs</td></tr>
<tr><td>Refund or return open</td><td>Freeze segmentation promos until refund or return closes</td><td>Open segmentation cases reset what the shopper tolerates</td></tr>
<tr><td>Repeated non-engagement</td><td>Remove chronic segmentation non-openers pre-complaint</td><td>Shields segmentation sender reputation and inboxing</td></tr>
<tr><td>SMS consent present</td><td>Segmentation texting respects time and frequency rules</td><td>Segmentation SMS risk exceeds email per complaint</td></tr>
<tr><td>Wholesale or B2B account</td><td>Segmentation wholesale accounts get dedicated messaging</td><td>B2B segmentation mis-sends risk contract breach</td></tr>
<tr><td>Free or disposable email domain</td><td>Gate segmentation journeys behind address verification</td><td>Segmentation bounces from junk signups hurt inboxing</td></tr>
<tr><td>Staff and test accounts</td><td>Segmentation QA profiles excluded from reporting</td><td>Segmentation reporting stays clean without test noise</td></tr>
<tr><td>Competitor or researcher signals</td><td>Treat segmentation snoops under normal consent policy</td><td>Segmentation one-offs breed audit gaps</td></tr>
<tr><td>Legacy list without timestamps</td><td>Segmentation sends to old lists need fresh opt-in</td><td>Segmentation compliance demands re-permission</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<h2 class="mt-12">Margin, app costs, and pricing for Segmentation</h2>
