<h2 class="mt-12">Governance and documentation for segmentation</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto mb-8"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Practice</th><th>Standard</th><th>Risk it prevents</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Flow ownership</td><td>Segmentation journeys each carry one owner</td><td>segmentation ghosts sending expired incentives</td></tr>
<tr><td>Naming convention</td><td>Segmentation prefixes by job and audience</td><td>Segmentation audits collapsing at peak</td></tr>
<tr><td>Change log</td><td>Log segmentation edits with date and rationale</td><td>segmentation performance drift with no log</td></tr>
<tr><td>Access control</td><td>Limit segmentation edit rights tightly</td><td>Segmentation accidents from excess access</td></tr>
<tr><td>Quarterly flow review</td><td>segmentation branch count kept lean</td><td>Overgrown segmentation journeys stalling ops</td></tr>
<tr><td>Incident runbook</td><td>segmentation kill steps plus alert list</td><td>Slow segmentation kill on broken sends</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<h2 class="mt-12">Peak season readiness for segmentation</h2>
<ol>
<li>For segmentation, freeze journey changes two weeks pre-peak.</li>
<li>Exercise each segmentation flow with live purchase, refund, support tests.</li>
<li>Check segmentation exits filter buyers and open cases.</li>
<li>Boost segmentation control groups before the surge.</li>
<li>For segmentation, pre-commit text timing and frequency limits.</li>
<li>Segmentation billing checked on peak math.</li>
<li>Segmentation placement watched every peak day.</li>
<li>Bank segmentation rollback plans ahead of sends.</li>
</ol>
<p>For segmentation, schedule quarter-one review before the first send. Writing segmentation suppression rules, discount caps, and escalation paths down in week one saves weeks of peak-season triage and hands newcomers a working segmentation playbook.</p>
<p>Close each segmentation quarter with a written ledger — segmentation sends shipped, suppressions honored, margin retained, failed bets — so segmentation vendor decisions rest on one shared evidence file, not scattered memory.</p>
